  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Creating a binary resource containing an RDF document can be achieved as follows:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "curl -X POST --data-binary \"@ore.rdf\" -H \"Content-Type: application/rdf+xml\" -H \"Slug: ore.rdf\" -H \"Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\\\"ore.rdf\\\"\" ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "http://localhost:8080/rest"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "http://localhost:8080/rest",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This creates a binary resource with mime type of application/rdf+xml as expected.  Retrieving its contents via GET results in an exception, however (stack trace attached). ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The problem is that ContentExposingResource is treating the binary content in a non-opaque fashion.  It appears to be parsing its contents as RDF, adding  (server-managed) triples from the associated object, and returning the union graph.  An exception is thrown at some point during this process.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A possible solution is to simply treat all binary resources opaquely as bytes, eliminating the exception for RDF.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
   "type": "doc",
   "version": 1
  },
