  "description": "<p>Creating a binary resource containing an RDF document can be achieved as follows:</p>\n\n<p>curl -X POST --data-binary \"@ore.rdf\" -H \"Content-Type: application/rdf+xml\" -H \"Slug: ore.rdf\" -H \"Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=\\\"ore.rdf\\\"\" <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest</a></p>\n\n<p>This creates a binary resource with mime type of application/rdf+xml as expected.  Retrieving its contents via GET results in an exception, however (stack trace attached). </p>\n\n<p>The problem is that ContentExposingResource is treating the binary content in a non-opaque fashion.  It appears to be parsing its contents as RDF, adding  (server-managed) triples from the associated object, and returning the union graph.  An exception is thrown at some point during this process.</p>\n\n<p>A possible solution is to simply treat all binary resources opaquely as bytes, eliminating the exception for RDF.</p>",
